1.  => join           - you must wait for the entire thread to finish.
    => CountDownLatch - you can proceed as soon as the important step is completed.

2. => join            - for n threads n joins needed
   => CountDownLatch  - single await() function is needed

3. => join            - cant use on thread pool
   => CountDownLatch  - can be used on thread pool



| Method                      | Purpose               |
| --------------------------- | --------------------- |
| `CountDownLatch(int count)` | initialize count      |
| `await()`                   | wait until count = 0  |
| `await(timeout, unit)`      | timed wait            |
| `countDown()`               | decrease count        |
| `getCount()`                | check remaining count |
| `toString()`                | debug info            |
